\pard\plain \sa240\sb320\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs36\b1 T}{\f1\fs36\b1 ardigrade culture and sampling}
\par\pard\plain \sa240\sb240\ltrch\loch {\f2\fs24\b0 The tardigrade }{\f3\fs24\b0\i1 Hypsibius dujardini}{\f2\fs24\b0  Z151 was purchased from Sciento (Manchester, UK) in August 2012, and its culture was maintained in the laboratory using the culture method previously described for }{\f3\fs24\b0\i1 Ramazzottius varieornatus}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref20"}{\fldrslt\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 2}}{\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 0}{\f2\fs24\b0 , with slight modifications. Briefly, tardigrades were fed }{\f3\fs24\b0\i1 Chlorella vulgaris}{\f2\fs24\b0  (Chlorella Industry) on 2% Bacto Agar (Difco) plates prepared with Volvic water, and the plates were incubated at 18 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u176\'B0C under constant dark conditions. Culture plates were renewed every 7~8 days. Adults with body lengths >300 \u956\'B5m were selected. Cultures were manually inspected every day to obtain freshly laid eggs within 24 h. Eggs were transferred to new plates for egg samples. Similarly, newly laid eggs were observed every day to obtain newly hatched juvenile samples. Anhydrobiotic samples were prepared by placing adult samples in a chamber maintained at 85% relative humidity for 48 h. Successful anhydrobiosis was assumed when >90% of the samples prepared in the same chamber recovered after rehydration.}
\par\pard\plain \sa240\sb320\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs36\b1 Genome sequencing}
\par\pard\plain \sa240\sb240\ltrch\loch {\f2\fs24\b0 An adult individual was selected and placed in a sterile agar plate with 1% penicillin streptomycin (Invitrogen) prepared with autoclaved Volvic water for 48 h without food to clear the gut content and remove surface microbes. After 48 h, the animal was repeatedly washed with Milli-Q water on a sterile nylon mesh with 30 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u956\'B5m pores (Millipore), and any surface microbes were observed at \u215\'D7500~\u215\'D71000 magnification under a microscope (VHX-5000, Keyence). The cleaned animal was transferred to a low-binding PCR tube with minimal water carry-over (<2 \u956\'B5l), to which a 200 \u956\'B5l genomic lysis buffer (Quick-gDNA MicroPrep kit, Zymo Research) with 0.5% beta-mercaptoethanol was added immediately. The animal was lysed using two freeze-thaw cycles of \u8722\'2D80 \u176\'B0C and 37 \u176\'B0C incubation, and genomic DNA was extracted following manufacturer\u8217\'92s protocol. Extracted DNA was then sheared to 550 bp target fragments with Covaris M220 using a 15 \u956\'B5l microTube, and the Illumina library was subsequently prepared using a Thruplex DNA-Seq kit (Rubicon Genomics) according to the manufacturer\u8217\'92s instructions. Thruplex kit was previously reported to be efficient in low-input sequencing}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref21"}{\fldrslt\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 2}}{\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 1}{\f2\fs24\b0 . The purified library was quantified using a Qubit Fluorometer (Life Technologies), and the size distribution was checked using TapeStation D1000 ScreenTape (Agilent Technologies). Library with sizes within the broad peak oberseved from TapeStation electropherogram between 400 and 1000 bp was selected by manually cutting them out of the agarose and purifying with a NucleoSpin Gel and PCR Clean-up kit (Clontech). The sample was then sequenced using one MiSeq v.3 600 cycles kit (Illumina) as 300 bp paired ends. Adapter sequences were removed using the MiSeq software (Illumina). In order to test the reproducibility of this single individual sequencing method, four more individuals were sequenced using the same procedures, except for the lysis step which was replaced by three freeze-thaw cycles of flash freezing with liquid nitrogen and 37 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u176\'B0C incubation, and the four libraries were multiplexed in a single MiSeq run. Genome extraction efficiency was assessed by extracting genomic DNA using the same method (with liquid nitrogen lysis) from 100 individuals with three replicates, and quantifying the amount using Qubit Fluorometer (Life Technologies).}
\par\pard\plain \sa240\sb320\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs36\b1 mRNA sequencing}
\par\pard\plain \sa240\sb240\ltrch\loch {\f2\fs24\b0 Active adults, adults in anhydrobiosis, eggs (1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 days after laying), and juveniles (1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 after hatching), were collected from the culture in three replicates and thoroughly washed with Milli-Q water on a sterile nylon mesh (Millipore). Each individual was placed in a low-binding PCR tube with minimal water carry-over (<2 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u956\'B5l). Pipette tips were used to crush animals by pressing them against the tube wall, and the individuals were then immediately lysed in TRIzol reagent (Life Technologies). RNA was extracted using a Direct-zol RNA kit (Zymo Research) following the manufacturer\u8217\'92s instructions. RNA quality was checked using High Sensitivity RNA ScreenTape on TapeStation (Agilent Technologies), and the mRNA was amplified via the SMART-Seq approach}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref22"}{\fldrslt\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 2}}{\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 2}{\f2\fs24\b0\super ,}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref23"}{\fldrslt\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 2}}{\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 3}{\f2\fs24\b0  using the SMARTer Ultra Low Input RNA Kit for Sequencing v.3 (Clontech). Illumina libraries were prepared using a KAPA HyperPlus Kit (KAPA Biosystems). A purified library was quantified using a Qubit Fluorometer (Life Technologies), and the size distribution was checked using TapeStation D1000 ScreenTape (Agilent Technologies). Libraries with sizes above 200 bp were selected by manually cutting them out of the agarose and purifying with a NucleoSpin Gel and PCR Clean-up kit (Clontech). The samples were then sequenced using a NextSeq 500 High Output Mode 75 cycles kit (Illumina) as single ends, with 48 multiplexed samples per run. Only two replicates were sequenced for the juvenile day 5 sample. Adapter sequences were removed, and sequences were demultiplexed using the bcl2fastq v.2 software (Illumina).}
\par\pard\plain \sa240\sb320\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs36\b1 Assembly and mapping of sequenced reads for technical validation}
\par\pard\plain \sa240\sb240\ltrch\loch {\f2\fs24\b0 Genome sequence reads were assembled }{\f3\fs24\b0\i1 de novo}{\f2\fs24\b0  using MaSuRCA 3.1.3 (ref. }{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref24"}{\fldrslt\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\cf3 2}}{\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\cf3 4}{\f2\fs24\b0 ) with a mean insert length of 350 and a standard deviation of 150. Because the minimum range of size selection was 400 bp, insert size without Illumina adapters roughly corresponds to this length. Moreover, we have confirmed by mapping our reads to the assembly of Koutsovoulos }{\f3\fs24\b0\i1 et al.}{\f2\fs24\b0  that the mean insert length was 363.5. Modifying this parameter to 550 bp produced identical assembly result, including the total number of scaffolds, average scaffold length, longest scaffold length, shortest scaffold length, scaffold N50, and scaffold N90. Only the total scaffold length was shortened by 551 bp. Using the assembly and genomic reads, the assembly of Boothby }{\f3\fs24\b0\i1 et al.}{\f2\fs24\b0  (tg.genome.fsa, hereafter referred to as the UNC assembly), one pair of the Boothby reads (TG-500- SIPE_1_sequence.txt and TG-500- SIPE_2_sequence.txt), the assembly of Koutsovoulos }{\f3\fs24\b0\i1 et al.}{\f2\fs24\b0  (nHd.2.3.abv500.fna, hereafter referred to as the Edinburgh assembly) and one pair of the Koutsovoulos reads (gHypdu_hiseq_pe_110427_3_1.fq and gHypdu_hiseq_pe_110427_3_2.fq) were mapped to assemblies in all combinations to assess the mapping rate. Mapping was performed using BWA v.0.7.11 MEM}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref25"}{\fldrslt\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 2}}{\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 5}{\f2\fs24\b0  with the default parameters, and the mapping percentage was calculated using the QualiMap build 11-11-13.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0 For the RNA-seq data, gene expression abundances were computed using the Kallisto software v.0.42.4 (ref. }{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref26"}{\fldrslt\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\cf3 2}}{\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\cf3 6}{\f2\fs24\b0 ) with accompanying sleuth utility using the Augustus-based gene prediction data of the Edinburgh assembly (nHd.2.3.1.aug.transcripts.fasta), with the following parameters: -b 100 --bias --single -l 400 -s 50. Overall gene expression profiles were scaled with scale() function and visualized as a heatmap for genes with TPM>1 using hierarchical clustering based on the Spearman correlation with hclust() and plotting using the ggplot2 utility in R}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201663#ref27"}{\fldrslt\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 2}}{\f2\fs24\b0\ul\ulc0\super\cf3 7}{\f2\fs24\b0 .}
\par\plain \f1\fs36\b1}